==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|hvar}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*hwar}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kʰvaːr/|lang=is}}
* {{IPA|/xʷaːr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|aːr|lang=is}}

===Adverb===
{{is-adv|-}}

# [[where]] (of location)
#: '''''Hvar''' áttu heima?''
#:: '''Where''' do you live?
#: '''''Hvar''' [[vera niðurkominn|er hann niðurkominn]]?''
#:: What’s become of him?
#: '''''Hvar''' í ósköpunum varstu, Óskar?''
#:: '''Where''' in heaven’s name were you, Óskar?

====Derived terms====
{{der-top}}
* {{l|is|finna hvar skórinn kreppir}} (to [[feel where the shoe pinches]])
* {{l|is|hér og hvar}} ([[here and there]])
{{der-mid}}
* {{l|is|sýna hvar Davíð keypti ölið}}
* {{l|is|víðast hvar}} (almost [[everywhere]])
{{der-bottom}}

